  "annotation": "SUPERSEDED - kept for the record. Two artefacts, both understood: (1) repeated-failed-login lateness=30s has two alerts at ~1,458 s and ~1,460 s: the host entered Modern Standby 2026-09-24 08:49:48 and exited 09:14:01 (24.2 min = 1,453 s), stalling the JVM and the driver together (Kernel-Power events 506/507); (2) password-spray lateness=0s shows a staircase of 8.5-22.6 s for the first ~10 incidents: the driver slept a fixed 12 s before starting, the JVM had not finished starting, and the early files queued behind it. The re-run gates on the first processed batch and holds the machine awake (scripts/bench/keep_awake.py)."
